egory one of the risk that can compromise both accuracy and trustworthiness in an ai system is it propensity to generate content that doe not align with information from input source also known a ungrounded content in march we introduced groundedness detection a feature that identifies and filter ungrounded content in ai output helping developer enhance the accuracy and usefulness of generative ai application by pinpointing response that lack a foundation in connected data source in september we launched a preview of correction a new capability within azure ai content safety s groundedness detection feature for our standalone api offering the correction capability corrects ungrounded ai output in real time before user encounter them to use groundedness detection a generative ai application must connect to grounding document or input source from which to base it output once the correction capability is enabled the detection of an ungrounded sentence trigger a new request to compare the flagged generated output against the grounding document the system will then either remove the sentence if no relevant content exists in the grounding document or rewrite the sentence to better align it with the grounding document also in september we launched our multimodal model in public preview in azure ai content safety the multimodal model analyzes material containing both image and text content to help our customer make application and service safer from harmful user generated or ai generated content key objective of the multimodal model include detecting harmful content across multiple modality analyzing both text and image including emojis to detect sexual violent and self harm content and content related to hate and unfairness within text image combination conducting contextual analysis across text and image the combined element of text and image may convey richer meaning than either mode alone the multimodal model can analyze text and image that occur together to detect subt