ense of the risk of ai system and their mitigation advocating for government to fund the agency and organization that could help to develop an effective third party testing regime e g in the united state nist the u ai safety institute the national ai research resource the usage of doe supercomputer for ai testing and so on encouraging government to build their own national research cloud like the national ai research resource in the u so that they can a develop independent capacity in academia and government to build study and test frontier ai system and b work third party testing a a key ingredient of ai policy anthropic side af on the science of evaluating ai system including those developed by private company like anthropic developing a testing regime and associated policy intervention based on the insight of industry government and academia is the best way to avoid societal harm whether deliberate or accidental from ai system how testing connects to our broader policy priority our overarching policy goal is to have appropriate oversight of the ai sector we believe this will mostly be achieved via there being an effective ecosystem for third party testing and evaluation of ai system here are some ai policy idea you can expect to see u advocating for in support of that greater funding for ai testing and evaluation in government effective testing and evaluation procedure are a necessary prerequisite of any effective form of ai policy we think that government should stand up and support institution that develop ai evaluation a well a bringing together industry academia and other stakeholder to agree on standard for the safety of ai system in the u we specifically advocate for greater funding for nist support greater evaluation of ai system through public sector infrastructure for doing ai research we urgently need to increase the number and breadth of people working to test and evaluate ai system for both current and future risk it s therefore crucial that government create experimental infrastructure to help academic researcher test out and evaluate frontier ai system and develop their own frontier system for third party testing a a key ingredient of ai policy anthropic side af beneficial purpose for more information see our support for a u national research cloud via the create ai act and our written senate testimony developing test for specific national security relevant capability we should know if ai system can be used in way that strengthen or if fielded by another entity weaken national security whereas the private sector and academia can develop the vast majority of test some testing and evaluation question relate to national security capability which are classified so only certain government are able to effectively evaluate them therefore we want to support u government effort to develop way of testing ai system for national security relevant capability we will also continue our own work to better understand the capability of our own system scenario planning and test development for increasingly advanced system our responsible scaling policy is designed to frontload work about evaluating and testing future hypothetical capability of ai system this is to ensure we have the relevant test to better assess and minimize accident and misuse risk from increasingly powerful ai system but we don t claim that our rsp delineates all the test that need to be run on increasingly powerful model a ai advance driven by growing computational power increase a broader set of actor should work to anticipate the future capability of ai system and develop test for them aspect of ai policy we believe are important to discus while developing our policy approach we ve also found ourselves returning again and again to a few specific issue such a openly third party testing a a key ingredient of ai policy anthropic side af accessible model and regulatory capture we ve outlined our current policy thinking below but recognize these are complicated