er on you get a text from her she asks you where you were born and your birth date and then she asks you about your family member name her request become more personal inquiring about your different email address and if you have a bank account protecting privacy explain discus a scenario about keeping private information private discus how do you respond to her text recommend discussing in small group or in pair but the discussion can be the entire class give your student a minute to consider their answer discus their response remember you do not know this person other than your online interaction while you play a video game why is she asking you for all of this personal information what is she going to do with all of this personal information let the student discus now if you do not feel comfortable sharing all of your personal information with someone you don t know should you share it with gemini discus their response during the lesson for many of u when a person we do not know asks for our personal information we become cautious a the risk of providing private information are clearer with technology especially ai the risk are less clear but we still need to be just a cautious there is a wide variety of ai available for you to use but they are not all created the same for example some ai may use the information you input into it including private information to train it model fortunately gemini is designed with privacy in mind when you use gemini a a young person there are protection in place to keep your information private the activity recording is off so gemini won t keep a record of what you input filter block any private information included in a prompt like your birth date from being reviewed or used to train gemini that being said you still shouldn t share your personal information with any ai model if time permit consider showing the student the google for education guide for ai and exploring some of the privacy practice with them key takeaway explain here are some example of private information to not share with ai full name social security number birth date home address phone number email address driver s license number passport number any financial or health information these include text and image please do not upload an image of your driver s license for example during the lesson all ai is created differently meaning you should take the time to review and understand their privacy practice even though there are privacy protection when you use gemini a a young person it s important to limit risk and build good habit by keeping personal information private remember keep private information private never enter personally identifiable information such a your social security number into generative ai system when in doubt consider whether you would share this information publicly tip use ai to boost your talent not replace them let s explore another scenario your classmate ahmed is behind with writing his art history report it is due during final week and he struggled managing his time to prepare for all of his exam and finish his project he know that soraya excels in the class so he asks if she can write the report for him since soraya ha completed her work already she agrees to help and write the rest of ahmed s paper academic integrity recommend discussing in small group or in pair but the discussion can be the entire class different school and teacher have their own academic integrity policy so it is important to know them and understand the guideline you need to follow ahmed s action are a breach of academic integrity academic integrity mean doing your work honestly in a way that is fair to you and others discus what is your initial reaction to this scenario what is problematic about this scenario student should identify that ahmed cheated he used another person s work a his own for a grade explain during the lesson key takeaway ahmed copying content from gemini and using it a his own is the same a asking soraya 