t were decided at the end of this phase the scenario wa conceptualized a a sto ryboard in slide deck that were shared and re ned with the group before being implemented by the vr studio quality assurance the nal development phase wa dedicated to polish the experience through qa testing session overall we carried out session involving volunteer tester besides asking them to report bug with the vr application we sent them an optional anonymous post session survey to evaluate the training e ectiveness and the leveraging virtual reality to enhance dei training at google chi may honolulu hawaii figure to avoid the suspension of disbelief e ect and increase realism the training location directly mimic google o ce importance of the post vr experience discussion tester lled it out noteworthy bug tester reported over problem through the course of the testing session those problem were prioritized and xed by the team with the help of the vr studio through an it erative design process between session beside expected software bug and nit report a few bug report emerged a noteworthy participant complained that hearing others wa detrimental to the experience during the vr training portion we ad dressed this issue by supplying headphone in future training session many participant experienced di culty with using the vr headset including complaint about the headset being too heavy and potentially not comfortable or usable by people with glass we addressed this issue by creating a playbook for facilitator that listed common issue and solution most participant were very sensitive to the delity of the simulation with a signi cant fraction of the bug reported being about visual glitch or simulation oddity those report included a character s teeth being distracting in an early version hand not being realistic enough the fact that one of the protagonist take a meeting from a common room which is unusual and the inability to nd a charac ter mentioned in a dialogue we improved the delity an