on a colleague is a victim of tokenism in the second a colleague is being dismis sive of others di erences including their food requirement driven by religious and cultural need a well a their pre ferred pronoun perspective the trainee experience the rst part a mandy an american white female and the nd part a hassan from bangalore india in both case the trainee is a bystander and ha the opportunity to interject in the conversation setting a hallway outside of a conference room in a u s google o ce part a and later at an o site part b dei concept racism stereotyping sexism representation tokenism and diversity learning objective this scenario help trainee recognize problematic conversation and allows them to step in in a tactful manner that highlight the issue scenario c performance and feedback synopsis this scenario explores the complexity of the power dynamic between manager and their report in the context of performance feedback through the lens of a female re port who ha moved to the country she s now working in asking to be put in charge of a project and having to ght preconception and biased comparison to other colleague perspective the trainee experience the rst part a magda a female software engineer from poland working out of dublin in the second part the trainee experience the dis cussion from the point of view of michael magda s manager who is working out of a google london o ce leveraging virtual reality to enhance dei training at google chi may honolulu hawaii figure screenshots of the four scenario developed for the training setting to meeting through video conferencing from a dublin home o ce meeting room and a google london conference room dei concept performance and feedback stereotyping power dynamic unconscious bias learning objective being able to recognize unconscious bi as during performance conversation to notice and reduce preconceived expectation based on those bias scenario d in group out group synopsis in this scenario a new team member is