e synchronized with blinkboard about how to assemble the circuit and how to wire different part of the circuit to the platform s i pin simultaneously the instructor would be able to inspect using an online dashboard if student correctly completed the circuit by inferring from their voltage graph whether the component were connected a expected this process is illustrated in fig like the workshop conducted in the high school a full analysis and reporting of the result from these experiment are beyond the scope of the paper however the collected data anecdotally demonstrate that completely online and remote physical computing education can be aided by using blinkboard for guiding and monitoring student progress we also think that blinkboard could have the potential for self practice of exercise at home although we currently do not have any data to support this claim and future work will be necessary to see the effect of using blinkboard a a self teaching aid ethic statement all human participant involved in our workshop signed an informed consent about collection of data and in case of minor the authorization wa provided by their parent,5318,0,[0.57666524 0.07590425 0.07174377 0.08562937 0.19005737]
