 for every they spend on google ad our first chief economist hal varian developed this estimate based on observed cost per click activity across a large sample of our advertiser his methodology wa published in the american economic review in may second we assume that overall business receive an average of five click on their search result for every one click on their ad this estimate wa developed by academic researcher bernard jansen and amanda spink based on sample search log data and published in the international journal of internet marketing and advertising in if search click brought in a much revenue for business a ad click these two assumption would imply that business would receive in profit for every they spend on google ad this is because if advertiser receive x a much value from google ad a they spend on google ad and they receive x a much value from google search a they do from google ad then the total profit they receive is x what they spend spend x spend spend spend however click through search result may not be a commercially valuable a ad click so we want to be conservative we will treat search click a being about a valuable a ad click this mean advertiser overall receive x the profit that they spend on google ad spend x x spend spend spend therefore we estimate that for every a business spends on google ad they receive in profit through google search and ad thus to derive the economic value received by advertiser we multiply our google ad revenue on search result in what advertiser spent by methodology google cloud we estimate the economic impact of google cloud based on the benefit that it generates for it user we rely on american company investment in google cloud for this calculation and make two core assumption first we assume that cloud technology is driving revenue growth and cost saving across both small and large organization second we assume that every dollar invested in cloud service by our user generates a net return the methodology we use doe not include any cloud service that are provided for free youtube ad like the economic impact of google search and ad we rely on two multiplier to estimate the economic impact of youtube ad based on analysis of actual campaign run on youtube first we assume that advertiser are willing to pay twice the amount of what they actually spend second we assume that brand advertiser receive on average more organic view on their channel than paid view then using similar method used to determine the economic value of google search and ad we were able to estimate a total surplus or profit for advertiser based on what they spent google network property youtube and google play the economic impact of google network property youtube and google play is based on the estimated amount we paid to publisher creator and developer in each u s state in for placing our ad next to their content and from app monetization google ad grant similarly the impact of google ad grant is the total amount spent by grant recipient in total economic value total economic value for each state is estimated a the economic activity provided to business publisher nonprofit creator and developer by google search google play youtube google cloud and google advertising tool in what s not included this is an attempt to estimate the economic impact of google s core search and advertising business in search and advertising we derive a conservative estimate of the impact of our tool on business publisher nonprofit developer and creator we leave out estimate such a the cost saving for consumer who are now able to find the information they need more easily than before we also do not include our employee economic impact or that of other major product such a google map and google analytics so while we are confident in our estimate consider them a lower end of google s true economic impact,8045,3,"[9.73395893e-309 1.00000000e+000 1.51654360e-308 2.29745061e-308
