uest without prompting further conversation we recognize that not all advertising implementation are equivalent more transparent or opt in approach where user explicitly choose to see sponsored content might avoid some of the concern outlined above but the history of ad supported product suggests that advertising incentive once introduced tend to expand over time a they become integrated into revenue target and product development blurring boundary that were once more clear cut we ve chosen not to introduce these dynamic into claude our approach anthropic is focused on business developer and helping our user flourish our business model is straightforward we generate revenue through enterprise contract and paid subscription and we reinvest that revenue into improving claude for our user this is a choice with tradeoff and we respect that other ai company might reasonably reach different conclusion expanding access to claude is central to our public benefit mission and we want to do it without selling our user attention or data to advertiser to that end we ve brought ai tool and training to educator in over country begun national ai education pilot with multiple government claude is a space to think anthropic anthropic side af and made claude available to nonprofit at a significant discount we continue to invest in our smaller model so that our free offering remains at the frontier of intelligence and we may consider lower cost subscription tier and regional pricing where there is clear demand for it should we need to revisit this approach we ll be transparent about our reason for doing so supporting commerce ai will increasingly interact with commerce and we look forward to supporting this in way that help our user we re particularly interested in the potential of agentic commerce where claude act on a user s behalf to handle a purchase or booking end to end and we ll continue to build feature that enable our user to find compare or buy product connect with business a