e little more than two year for each state s aui to close most of the gap to the anthropic economic index report figure anthropic ai usage index aui across the u august v and november v by comparing the aui in november with it value in august we can estimate the implied rate of diffusion of claude usage within the u under a model of proportional convergence toward a steady state in which aui for all u state the estimated elasticity can be used to calculate the pace of diffusion see text for more detail our range of estimate implies a pace of regional convergence of aui in year a concern with estimating convergence this way is that our aui estimate are subject to sampling noise and other variation unrelated to diffusion this can produce classical attenuation bias even if aui is not actually changing our estimate of could end up meaningfully below one to address this we estimate the model by two stage least square sl instrumenting the log of aui in august with the composition of each state s workforce measured by it proximity to overall claude usage pattern the logic behind this instrument is that workforce composition is a strong the anthropic economic index report predictor of claude usage relevance but being measured independently is expected to be uncorrelated with sampling noise in our aui estimate validity a noted above state with more worker in high claude usage role do tend to have systematically higher usage per caput the sl estimate imply modestly slower convergence unweighted and when weighting by each state s working age population however these estimate are less precise and only the former is statistically distinguishable from at the level despite implying a slower convergence than ols the sl estimate still imply rapid diffusion just four to five year for the log deviation of each state s aui to shrink by that said our estimate are based on just three month of data and while the sl specification may help address sampling noise considerable uncertainty remains we will revisit this question of the pace of diffusion in future report a with previous report all our analysis is based on privacy preserving analysis throughout the report we analyze a random sample of m conversation from claude ai free pro and max conversation we also refer to this a consumer data since it mostly represents consumer use and m transcript from our first party p api traffic we also refer to this a enterprise data since it mostly represents enterprise use both sample come from november to november we continue to manage data according to our privacy and retention policy and our analysis is consistent with our term policy and contractual agreement for p api data each record is a prompt response pair from our sample period which in some instance is mid session for multi turn interaction the share of conversation on claude ai that were classified into neither automation nor augmentation category fell from to see for example kalanyi et al second a the technology mature and the number of related job grows hiring spread geographically this process is very slow taking around year to disperse fully the anthropic economic index report with our bottom up analysis of p api traffic we see claude used to generate personalized b b cold sale email analyze email and draft reply for business correspondence build and maintain invoice processing system classify and categorize email into predefined label and manage calendar scheduling meeting coordination and appointment booking at a high level we distinguish between automation and augmentation mode of using claude automation encompasses interaction pattern focused on task completion directive user give claude a task and it completes it with minimal back and forth feedback loop user automate task and provide feedback to claude a needed augmentation focus on collaborative interaction pattern learning user ask claude for information or explanation about various topic task iteration user iterate on task collaboratively