ctivity we calculate task level efficiency gain a the log difference between human time without ai and with ai there are certainly other way to adjust based on task reliability if task in our sample are composed of sub task with heterogeneous ai applicability and worker optimally deploy ai only on sub task where it is effective then scaling the efficiency gain by the success rate capture the extensive margin of ai adoption within a task we use a ce constant elasticity of substitution production function to aggregate task level time saving to economy wide productivity impact the elasticity parameter governs how easily worker can substitute between task when we apply hulten s theorem directly the aggregate productivity gain equal the wage share weighted sum of log speedup across task for we use a two level aggregation first within each occupation we compute an occupation level speedup a a ce aggregate of task speedup weighted by time fraction using then we apply hulten s theorem to these occupation level speedup when complement productivity gain are bottlenecked by task with the smallest speedup when substitute worker can specialize in task where ai provides the largest speedup amplifying aggregate gain for task without observed ai speedup data we assume no productivity change we thank pascual restrepo for suggesting this particular exercise the anthropic economic index report concluding remark this fourth anthropic economic index report introduces economic primitive foundational characteristic of ai use that show how claude is used by both consumer and firm we use claude to estimate the extent to which usage varies along these dimension these measure are directionally accurate and taken together provide important signal even if individual classification are imperfect our finding carry significant implication for how ai will reshape economy and labor market notably claude tends to be used more and appears to provide greater productivity boost on task that require high