Level_2_Meso,Anthropic,Anthropic partners with CodePath to bring Claude to the US’s largest collegiate computer science program \ Anthropic.pdf,"15.04.2026, 20.56 Anthropic partners with CodePath to bring Claude to the US’s largest collegiate computer science program \ Anthropic Side 1 af 3 https://www.anthropic.com/news/anthropic-codepath-partnership Anthropic partners with CodePath to bring Claude to the US’s largest collegiate computer science program Anthropic is partnering with CodePath, the nation’s largest provider of collegiate computer science education, to redesign its coding curriculum as AI reshapes the field of software development. CodePath will put Claude and Claude Code at the center of its courses and career programs, giving more than 20,000 students at community colleges, state schools, and HBCUs access to frontier AI tools as part of their education. Over 40% of CodePath students come from families earning under $50,000 a year, and CodePath aims to provide them with industry-vetted courses and access to career networks traditionally reserved for students at wealthier institutions. What we’re building CodePath is integrating Claude into its AI courses—including Foundations of AI Engineering, Applications of AI Engineering, and AI Open-Source Capstone—so students can learn to build with tools like Claude Code and contribute to real-world open-source projects. In the fall of 2025, over 100 CodePath students piloted Claude Code to contribute to open-source projects like GitLab, Puter, and Dokploy. Students said they found the experience both valuable and challenging. “Claude Code was instrumental in my learning process, especially since I came into the project with very little experience in the programming languages used in the repository [including TypeScript and Node.js],” said 15.04.2026, 20.56 Anthropic partners with CodePath to bring Claude to the US’s largest collegiate computer science program \ Anthropic Side 2 af 3 https://www.anthropic.com/news/anthropic-codepath-partnership Laney Hood, CodePath student and computer science major at Texas Tech University. In January, Howard University announced a redesigned Intro to Artificial Intelligence course, developed in partnership with CodePath and the Thurgood Marshall College Fund. The course gives students experience with Claude-assisted software development, preparing them for the type of work that now defines entry-level engineering roles. It represents the first time CodePath’s applied AI curriculum is being offered for academic credit at a university. “We now have the technology to teach in two years what used to take four,” said Michael Ellison, Co-founder and CEO of CodePath. “But speed for some and not others just widens inequality. Partnering with Anthropic means our students learn to build with Claude from day one, at institutions that have historically been overlooked. This results in better outcomes for our students and a fundamentally different answer to who gets to shape the AI economy.” Beyond the classroom, Anthropic and CodePath will collaborate on public research exploring how AI is changing coding education and the dynamics of economic opportunity. We’ll share what we learn from students, educators, and industry leaders about what’s working—and what isn’t—as AI changes how people build technical skills and enter the workforce. A broader commitment to AI education This partnership builds on Anthropic’s work to put AI tools in the hands of educators and students. We’re partnering with the American Federation of Teachers (AFT) to offer free AI training to their 1.8 million members across the US. In Iceland, we launched one of the world’s first national AI education pilots with the Ministry of Education and Children, giving teachers across the country access to Claude. In Rwanda, we’re working with the government and ALX to bring a Claude-powered learning 15.04.2026, 20.56 Anthropic partners with CodePath to bring Claude to the US’s largest collegiate computer science program \ Anthropic Side 3 af 3 https://www.anthropic.com/news/anthropic-codepath-partnership companion to hundreds of thousands of students and young professionals across Africa. We also signed the White House’s “Pledge to America’s Youth: Investing in AI Education,” committing to expand AI education nationwide through investments in cybersecurity education, the Presidential AI Challenge, and a free AI curriculum for educators. The tools changing how software is built shouldn’t only be available to students at well-resourced universities. With CodePath, they won’t be.",anthropic partner with codepath to bring claude to the u s largest collegiate computer science program anthropic side af anthropic partner with codepath to bring claude to the u s largest collegiate computer science program anthropic is partnering with codepath the nation s largest provider of collegiate computer science education to redesign it coding curriculum a ai reshapes the field of software development codepath will put claude and claude code at the center of it course and career program giving more than student at community college state school and hbcus access to frontier ai tool a part of their education over of codepath student come from family earning under a year and codepath aim to provide them with industry vetted course and access to career network traditionally reserved for student at wealthier institution what we re building codepath is integrating claude into it ai course including foundation of ai engineering application of ai engineering and ai open source capstone so student can learn to build with tool like claude code and contribute to real world open source project in the fall of over codepath student piloted claude code to contribute to open source project like gitlab puter and dokploy student said they found the experience both valuable and challenging claude code wa instrumental in my learning process especially since i came into the project with very little experience in the programming language used in the repository including typescript and node j said anthropic partner with codepath to bring claude to the u s largest collegiate computer science program anthropic side af laney hood codepath student and computer science major at texas tech university in january howard university announced a redesigned intro to artificial intelligence course developed in partnership with codepath and the thurgood marshall college fund the course give student experience with claude assisted software development preparing them for the type of work that now defines entry level engineering role it represents the first time codepath s applied ai curriculum is being offered for academic credit at a university we now have the technology to teach in two year what used to take four said michael ellison co founder and ceo of codepath but speed for some and not others just widens inequality partnering with anthropic mean our student learn to build with claude from day one at institution that have historically been overlooked this result in better outcome for our student and a fundamentally different answer to who get to shape the ai economy beyond the classroom anthropic and codepath will collaborate on public research exploring how ai is changing coding education and the dynamic of economic opportunity we ll share what we learn from student educator and industry leader about what s working and what isn t a ai change how people build technical skill and enter the workforce a broader commitment to ai education this partnership build on anthropic s work to put ai tool in the hand of educator and student we re partnering with the american federation of teacher aft to offer free ai training to their million member across the u in iceland we launched one of the world s first national ai education pilot with the ministry of education and child giving teacher across the country access to claude in rwanda we re working with the government and